{
  "id": "30531_hakobidasu",
  "headword": "{運|はこ}び{出|だ}す",
  "reading": "はこびだす",
  "romaji": "hakobidasu",
  "part_of_speech": "verb (godan)",
  "gloss": "to carry out; to haul out; to remove",
  "definitions": [
    {
      "sense_number": 1,
      "gloss": "to carry out; to haul out",
      "explanation": "To carry something from inside a place to outside it. The 〜{出|だ}す half supplies the outward direction, so the focus is on getting the object out rather than on where it ends up."
    }
  ],
  "examples": [
    {
      "id": "30531_hakobidasu_ex1",
      "japanese": "{荷物|にもつ}を{運|はこ}び{出|だ}す。",
      "english": "To carry the luggage out.",
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ],
      "has_audio": false,
      "notes": null
    },
    {
      "id": "30531_hakobidasu_ex2",
      "japanese": "{机|つくえ}を{廊下|ろうか}に{運|はこ}び{出|だ}してください。",
      "english": "Please carry the desk out into the hallway.",
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ],
      "has_audio": false,
      "notes": null
    },
    {
      "id": "30531_hakobidasu_ex3",
      "japanese": "{倒|たお}れた{人|ひと}を、{数人|すうにん}がかりで{建物|たてもの}の{外|そと}へ{運|はこ}び{出|だ}した。",
      "english": "Several of them together carried the collapsed person out of the building.",
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ],
      "has_audio": false,
      "notes": null
    }
  ],
  "notes": "TRANSITIVITY:\n- Transitive: {荷物|にもつ}を{運|はこ}び{出|だ}す. The starting point takes から or を, the destination に or へ.\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {家具|かぐ}を{運|はこ}び{出|だ}す: to move furniture out\n- {倉庫|そうこ}から{運|はこ}び{出|だ}す: to haul out of the warehouse\n- {負傷者|ふしょうしゃ}を{運|はこ}び{出|だ}す: to carry out the injured\n\nSIMILAR WORDS:\n- {運|はこ}び{込|こ}む: to carry in — the opposite direction\n- {持|も}ち{出|だ}す: to take out — often means removing without permission, or bringing up a topic",
